 Colloid Sci</source><year>1955</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>246</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Twomey</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of constrained linear inversion and an iterative non-linear algorithm applied to the indirect estimation of particle size distributions</article-title><source>J Comput Phys</source><year>1975</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>188</fpage><lpage>200</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Hiller</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Quantitative deposition of ultrafine stable particles in the human respiratory tract</article-title><source>J Appl Physiol</source><year>1985</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>223</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3968012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yeh</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cuddihy</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Phalen</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Comparisons of calculated respiratory tract deposition of particles based on the proposed NCRP model and the new ICRP model</article-title><source>Aerosol Sci Technol</source><year>1996</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>40</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>WRAS sampler website</collab><year>2006</year><comment>Available at <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.naneum.com">http://www.naneum.com</ext-link>. Accessed January 2009</comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>